# Default UUID for Supabase inserts

When inserting a record into a Supabase table, if a UUID column must be populated (`created_by`, `modified_by`, or any other required UUID that is not generated), use this value unless the user specifies a different id:

```text
ec092de5-1bd7-4321-ba9c-f8cbfccb5341
```

```sql
-- ✅ GOOD
insert into catalog.file_extension (code, value, created_by, modified_by)
values (7, '.svg', 'ec092de5-1bd7-4321-ba9c-f8cbfccb5341', 'ec092de5-1bd7-4321-ba9c-f8cbfccb5341');

-- ❌ BAD — invented or omitted UUID when the column needs a value
insert into catalog.file_extension (code, value, created_by, modified_by)
values (7, '.svg', gen_random_uuid(), gen_random_uuid());
```

- Do not use this as a generated primary key
- Do not replace a UUID the user explicitly provides
